            <ArticleTitle>Roux-en-Y intussusception after pediatric liver transplant - A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>855-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/petr.12743</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Small bowel obstruction in a pediatric patient following liver transplant often results from adhesions, hernias, or post-transplant lymphoproliferative disease. Here, we present an unusual and previously unreported entity - Roux-en-Y intussusception in an eight-yr-old female several years after liver transplantation. Although a rare complication, Roux-en-Y intussusception should be considered as a potential etiology in the patient presenting with bowel obstruction, with specific attention to acute presentation accompanying jaundice.</AbstractText>
